  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275040/assets/a5683d7d99771b1595a4c8493e65776c5190b3e9784f94db0ff0476967a89ccb.png)\n\nThe ellipse shown above has integer-length axes.\nFind the length of the major axis of the ellipse.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The major axis is the longest diameter of the ellipse, which is the line segment bounded by the points $(-1,0)$ and $(-1,6).$ So, the length of the major axis is $6-0=6.$",
